  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Burkina Faso II - Gender Integration Project - Non-allocated Funds activity: Due Diligence funding is used to obtain sufficient information to evaluate, assess and appraise projects during program development, effectively oversee and monitor program implementation, conduct quality assurance, and then evaluate the results of the project once complete. In this particular project, due diligence funds were used to hire external technical assistance to support MCC&apos;s assessment of the MCA&apos;s projects for social impact, documented in the Environmental and Social Impact Assessment, and oversee the social impact risks throughout implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
